### Accessibility & UX requirements

Every `<input>` and `<textarea>` must have an associated `<label>` connected by `htmlFor` / `id`. The EN/AR badges inside labels are decorative spans and must have `aria-hidden="true"`. The section card's save button shows a visible focus ring on keyboard focus. All drag-and-drop interactions in the NavigationEditor have keyboard alternatives: arrow keys to reorder when the drag handle is focused. The legal page textareas have a character count displayed below them in muted text (e.g. "1,240 characters"). The color hex input shows a red border when the entered value is not a valid hex color.

